{"title":"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the surface of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sphere\" title=\"Sphere\">sphere</a> with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. It is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde1774a06facbf7b3c05e82bc4ed9bd41cd786a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace7328133fbaac6396a6e5fc9fa65f335320cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a20686d6a518df9865b1b3d8abb870bdeaad690f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, and that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7383d5e36f82cf40da8500c44b15493d445842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m\\sqrt{n}}k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2c2d940b225be2cb344eddb55d6cc720d2778f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the plane of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/4631be2d820474d4f6fec03acedb2817f135fd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e75efb6abaae407233baf1ad552792b2982c9757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b314163f3d7b82d78944283deda01130ab862d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b538b928a06b84344fe1897ce659d5a3da34fc3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DA^2=DB^2=DC^2=20^2-OD^2\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/187bedab0f211bda7a3af5a752ecd3176806f778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=DB=DC$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_Formula\" title=\"Heron&#39;s Formula\">Heron's Formula</a> the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is (alternatively, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/20697823da9ea9148dbc3b247e1758c6baa01188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-14-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangle may be split into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a69890fe7f8a233e9346bc908b99d65d084274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-12-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangles</a>):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88fedef2fa3ba80f57bd8c4b9c5d8043adc79a60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \\sqrt{21(21-15)(21-14)(21-13)} = 84\\]\" width=\"547\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/3930c90edbe133a3a6bf1e68c87654f8b99ad291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac{abc}{4K}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, we know that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumradius\" title=\"Circumradius\">circumradius</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70a5d149bd7a2c2a5c0adfdac523dafb1c952fdd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = \\frac{abc}{4K} = \\frac{(13)(14)(15)}{4(84)} = \\frac{65}{8}\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> again,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/27629451a7064a00efed8b7109d142852aebab3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OD = \\sqrt{20^2-R^2} = \\sqrt{20^2-\\frac{65^2}{8^2}} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{95}}{8}.\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>So the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c47d3c295b2e61f0e77fc984d702d0f9a95332e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15+95+8=\\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Vectors)\">Solution 2 (Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know the radii to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> form a triangular pyramid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91381b367f9753ded66ab981c7451f2cb117578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OABC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. We know the lengths of the edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a82cad8965f76f79389c7ee100c3174d1c7071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = OB = OC = 20$\" width=\"176\" height=\"13\" />. First we can break up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> into its two component right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a69890fe7f8a233e9346bc908b99d65d084274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-12-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Let the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis be perpendicular to the base and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis run along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> occupy the other dimension, with the origin as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We look at vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e77bb510b99a851bde2c668e4ef665ba76b2622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is isoceles we know the vertex is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, hence it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units along the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis. Hence for vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, in form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546801a1557a3c79f1bf7e4a9e5cbdf8432d9343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;x,y,z&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e4079329a363ec7d5103c65ef189c7b3981a169a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;7, h, l&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the height (answer) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is the component of the vertex along the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> axis. Now on vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> axis, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb3fa1151e58a33589dc62fdeffa3cb8990467b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;-2, h, 12- l&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />. We know both vector magnitudes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc3c06a6c3d68f7e44ceba4073b860a75512d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15\\sqrt{95} }{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" />, so Answer = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c851b8731ef9deac914acfd0c0e569472391ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> is actually <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4af18d1da67fe94d07a6abe9c2156dfeda61532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left&lt; 2, -h, 12-l \\right&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />. ~fermat_sLastAMC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> forms a  right triangle with the circumradius of the triangle and the radius of the sphere. \n</p><p><br />\nThe hypotenuse has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, since it is the radius of the sphere.\n</p><p><br />\nThe circumradius of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0637989904ee8de568957d00385b3d878898928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{65}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, so the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f9d530a896e1a353db4f90372a7d822eedcc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20^2-(\\frac{65}{8})^2} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{95}}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"191\" height=\"45\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f60d2d18424535721ec49cfcc8425daea82e3d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15+95+8 = \\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-skibbysiggy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II\" title=\"2000 AIME II\">2000 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AIM